I ran in to this problem and it complained about size_t being defined at
different sizes or some such. The way I did it was

1. copy all the *.c and *.h files to the existing NH3.0j 'src' directory
2. changed the config.h and system.h in the 'src' directory (not the 'include'
   directory)  to reflect the environment (unix, BSD etc)
3. run make in the src directory
4. when it complains, edit out the ^M in the offending file (easily done in
   emacs with a quick macro)
5. repeat 4 until successful

